<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/4th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Issus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">333 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Issus · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Issus was fought in 333 BCE near the Gulf of Issus in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darius-iii">Darius III</a>. Alexander won, and Darius fled, leaving his family to be captured. The victory opened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus.jpg" alt="Battle of Issus" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Issus_mosaic_-_Museo_Archeologico_Nazionale_-_Naples_2013-05-16_16-25-06_BW.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
